WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.160
When you think of the SCP Foundation, you
probably think of the organization being primarily

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.520
based in the United States.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.470
After all, many of the anomalies we cover
here on SCP Explained happen to take place

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.400
in America, so it’s easy to lose sight of
the bigger picture.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.380
The fact of the matter is that the anomalous
is not just confined to the United States,

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.330
and if it were, the Foundation would have
a much easier time doing its job than it actually

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:26.330
does.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.359
Unfortunately for the Foundation, it’s not
just the U.S that they have to focus their

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:33.130
efforts on, it’s the entire world.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:38.840
That’s right, no matter where you are on
earth, no matter how far you travel the threat

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.760
of being the victim to an unsuspecting anomalous
incident remains the same.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.150
Even on your family vacation to Disney World.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:52.120
Of course, the Foundation’s mission is massively
expensive too, with each object requiring

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.420
not only significant resources to capture,
but even more to effectively contain and study

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.190
over a long period of time.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:04.369
And then you have the utilities of each site,
keeping the power on and the water running.

00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:08.770
Or what about actually paying the hard-working
SCP personnel who put their lives on the line

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:09.979
every day?

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:15.179
How about keeping global reconnaissance as
a watchful eye in case talk of any unnatural

00:01:15.179 --> 00:01:18.659
incidents start making the rounds in the ordinary
world?

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:23.069
What about maintaining a standing army of
trained task force operatives, far deadlier

00:01:23.069 --> 00:01:26.170
than any other military force on the planet?

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.760
Resources to cover-up events as soon as they
happen?

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.100
Field agents?

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.100
Database expenses?

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.310
It’s unimaginable to think of the costs
of operating the Foundation in one country,

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.330
let alone on a global scale.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.670
So, how do they manage this heavy responsibility?

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:47.289
How does the SCP Foundation divide up its
resources accordingly, as well as raise enough

00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:49.689
money to continue operating?

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:53.810
Think about it, if you were an organization
having to cover the entire globe in service

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:59.240
of protecting humanity from the anomalous,
what would be the best way of managing your

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.240
resources?

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.179
First, you’d make sure you were backed by
the richest of the rich, who could use some

00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:06.819
of their personal wealth to fund your goals.

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:11.659
Well, that’s the Overseer Council, the group
at the top of the Foundation composed of some

00:02:11.659 --> 00:02:14.830
of the most affluent and wealthy individuals
in the world.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.750
Second, you’d make sure you had a means
of generating revenue.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:23.160
The Foundation can’t exactly open itself
for donations from the public, and it can’t

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.810
issue taxes, but it can have others do that
for them.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.710
Cover-up businesses and sourcing funding from
the governments of the world, either legitimately

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:37.439
or through blackmailing, are two surefire
ways to keep the cash flowing endlessly.

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:41.300
Who knows how many fortune 500 companies are
actually owned by the Foundation?

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.319
There’s a lot of money in the world to go
around, but someone needs to capitalize on

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:47.840
it in order to get it.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.020
But the most important way to manage global
resources is decentralization.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:57.069
Remember what we said about the perception
of the Foundation being U.S based?

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:01.939
Well, it’s true that the Foundation had
its origins in the United States, and the

00:03:01.939 --> 00:03:06.650
country is the center of a large number of
containment efforts, but the english speaking

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.189
branch of the Foundation is far from the only
one.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:15.450
Allow us to introduce International Branches,
or -INT, for short.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:20.280
The Foundation likes to codify its various
branches based on the majority language spoken

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:25.620
there, so the English speaking branch would
cover nations such as the United States, Canada,

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.900
and parts of Europe.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.480
While in regions where Chinese is spoken,
the Chinese branch presides over the territory.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:36.660
Truly, the containment of the anomalous is
a global effort, with at least one Foundation

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.939
site located in each country.

00:03:38.939 --> 00:03:41.599
Africa, India, Japan, Latin America.

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:45.790
There isn’t a part of the world that the
Foundation doesn’t have covered, and for

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.579
good reason too.

00:03:47.579 --> 00:03:51.190
Anomalous objects can be discovered anywhere
and everywhere.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:56.140
Having locations near all major population
centers isn’t just a luxury of having unlimited

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.680
funding, it's the very thing that necessitates
such funding.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.280
And with International branches adhering to
their own policies, holding their own personnel,

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.810
and speaking their own languages, it should
come as no surprise that they have their own

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.370
database of SCP objects too.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:18.120
That’s right, each branch has an archive
of files of their own, written based on objects

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.280
contained in their respective country.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.630
Imagine being the guy who’s just finishing
reading all of the files currently existing

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.840
in the English database, when you realize
you then have to drudge through several more

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:33.750
databases filled with thousands upon thousands
of files just to be the completionist your

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.289
heart wants you to be.

00:04:35.289 --> 00:04:39.590
It’s a time consuming task, but that’s
what we’re here for, and today we’re going

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:47.160
to boost your own international database with
coverage of SCP-007-INT, an anomaly sourced

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.690
from the Foundation’s global database!

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.669
It all started in Massarosa, Italy.

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:54.720
A medium-sized town located just outside Pisa.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.450
It’s not famous for much, well, outside
of hosting the annual Massarosa international

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.590
piano competition, which we should remind
you that we’re all very excited about this

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:07.169
year considering Dr. Clef himself has decided
he’d enter.

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:12.110
But enough about Agent Ukulele's wild pianist
skills, let’s get back to the story at hand.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:17.009
A contingent of Mobile Task Force operatives
sourced from a squad dubbed “Smoking Anomalous

00:05:17.009 --> 00:05:21.259
Snakes”, who belonged to the Foundation’s
Italian branch, were stationed in the town

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:23.009
for the past week.

00:05:23.009 --> 00:05:27.650
Given that Massarosa is smaller than the average
city, with a population numbering just over

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:33.490
22,000, these operatives had to take extra
precaution as to not give away their presence.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:38.190
In a town where everyone knows everyone, a
gaggle of unfamiliar faces making their way

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.569
through could set off proverbial alarms in
the local population.

00:05:42.569 --> 00:05:46.910
The Foundation operatives were there for a
single purpose - to source the production

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:50.190
of anomalous weaponry rumored to be occurring
throughout the region.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:53.360
Now, why is this a problem in the first place?

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:58.379
As technology advances, war changes along
with it, sometimes necessitating the need

00:05:58.379 --> 00:06:02.349
for more efficient weapons and inspiring their
development.

00:06:02.349 --> 00:06:04.889
Spears to deal with invading tribes on land.

00:06:04.889 --> 00:06:08.039
Horses and chariots to rush those with spears.

00:06:08.039 --> 00:06:10.419
Bows and arrows to combat horses.

00:06:10.419 --> 00:06:15.849
War has always made use of new technology
to make combat more efficient and deadly.

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:18.450
And anomalous weaponry is no different.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:22.930
After all, not every paranormal organization
holds the same ethos as the Foundation’s

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:25.800
Secure, Contain, Protect mentality.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.200
There are many groups of interest, such as
the dreaded Chaos Insurgency or the Foundation’s

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:35.379
greatest rival, the Global Occult Coalition,
that would be more than happy to utilize research

00:06:35.379 --> 00:06:38.160
into the anomalous for military purposes.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.479
And who can blame them?

00:06:39.479 --> 00:06:44.169
With anomalous weaponry, situations can be
resolved and enemies eradicated easier and

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:46.129
deadlier than ever before.

00:06:46.129 --> 00:06:50.099
Up against a world that doesn’t abide by
their mission, even the Foundation is forced

00:06:50.099 --> 00:06:54.720
to utilize anomalous weaponry, albeit on a
smaller scale.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.319
Take Task Force Alpha-9 “Last Hope”, a
squad made up entirely of SCP objects, such

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:08.290
as SCP-105, Iris Thompson, and SCP-4494, the
world’s greatest arbiter of vigilante justice,

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.220
otherwise known as The Spectre.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:17.220
Even Mobile Task Forces, such as Samsara,
a group of heavily augmented cybernetic super-soldiers,

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.830
make use of anomalous weaponry to further
advance their efficiency on the field.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:26.560
After all, Task Forces spend their time combating
anomalies in the field, it only makes sense

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:29.159
to fight fire with fire, so to speak.

00:07:29.159 --> 00:07:34.610
Third party sellers and producers of anomalous
weaponry often provide the technology to established

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:39.730
groups of interest, so the Foundation getting
the jump on a distribution center in Massarosa,

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.850
Italy was a strategic move on the part of
the Foundation.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:47.090
They weren’t sure of the exact details,
but their sources tipped them off about a

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:52.970
gang of fascist, neo-Nazis in the area working
on supplying anomalous weaponry to the criminal

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.090
underworld.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:58.789
Its bad enough that the trigger-happy radicals
at the Chaos Insurgency have access to anomalous

00:07:58.789 --> 00:08:03.780
means of destruction, imagine if every two-bit
gangster and minor criminal had their hands

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:09.509
on something as deadly as an SCP object, and
they could acquire even more powerful equipment

00:08:09.509 --> 00:08:10.759
if they wanted.

00:08:10.759 --> 00:08:14.810
If the fascists made their money, who knows
where their anomalous weaponry would wind

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:15.810
up?

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:19.610
The Foundation wasn’t sure what they were
manufacturing, but they were positive that

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.040
it wasn’t good.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.099
Their source explicitly described it as a
weapon that could change the course of war

00:08:25.099 --> 00:08:29.310
as they understood it, a living, breathing
shield.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:33.370
Naturally, the Foundation was just as interested
in potentially finding a purpose for this

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:38.599
mystery weapon as they were in taking it out
of the hands of the black market suppliers.

00:08:38.599 --> 00:08:40.979
What uses could it hold in the field?

00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:44.829
Could it provide an extra layer of protection
for the Foundation’s operatives?

00:08:44.829 --> 00:08:49.310
The operatives were compiled from a vanguard
and reconnaissance team, and were the only

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:52.950
ones the resource strained Italian branch
had available for the job.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.870
They spent days combing through the town until
they stumbled upon what they believed to be

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.470
a hideout for the gang.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:03.220
While attempting to investigate, a mysterious
man ran out in front of the team, darting

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:05.450
towards them from across the street.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:09.800
The team went to shoot, but hesitated after
realizing that the man was accompanied by

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:15.089
a mysterious silver balloon-like entity ominously
floating above his shoulder.

00:09:15.089 --> 00:09:20.360
Not only that, but he was wearing a full suit
of protective equipment, almost like a bee

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.370
keeper’s suit.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.890
The operatives opened fire at the unidentified
target, but before their bullets could make

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:31.370
contact, the silver balloon began bubbling,
and spread itself across the man’s body,

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.560
like a protective sheet.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:35.990
It was then that they knew they found their
living shield.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:40.540
The bullets slid right off of the man, hitting
the liquid covering him and immediately being

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.029
negated by its anomalous properties.

00:09:43.029 --> 00:09:48.410
Then, before the team could react, the liquid
shot forward, detaching from the man’s body

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.700
and latching onto a Foundation operative.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:55.220
The silver gel began to writhe and constrict,
attempting to absorb the operative through

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:56.810
his protective gear.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:10:00.930
In a quick executive decision, the team lead
made the choice to put the operative, who

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:04.530
was in the midst of being absorbed by the
gel, out of his misery.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:08.510
After all, they couldn’t take risks when
dealing with an unknown anomaly, especially

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:12.720
one that they already knew was being utilized
as a deadly weapon.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:17.120
As soon as the body dropped dead, both the
liquid and the gang member took off through

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.310
the streets, and the Foundation gave pursuit.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:24.070
The Foundation chased the man through the
narrow, maze-like streets of the town, with

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:28.550
the silver liquid tailing after them and attempting
to absorb even more operatives.

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:30.910
Thankfully, the gel wasn’t fast.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.810
The man, however, was another story.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:39.310
The operatives chased and chased, indiscriminately
unloading a salvo of bullets into the general

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:40.310
area.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:43.640
A few struck, puncturing the man’s skin
and causing him to bleed.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:48.120
Following the trail of blood, the Foundation
was able to corner him into a street alley.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:54.029
But then, all of a sudden, the gel burst through
the concrete wall the man was backed up against,

00:10:54.029 --> 00:10:56.230
the anomaly now larger than ever.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:11:00.630
The goo reconnected with the man, shielding
him from the Foundation’s firepower and

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.160
allowing him to run away and escape.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:07.790
The Foundation briefly retreated and reconvened
with their superiors to try to find the best

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.660
strategy to move forward.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:14.490
They then took to the streets again, searching
for the man and any trace of the anomaly.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:18.899
They found bits of the liquid strewn through
the streets, squirming and writhing.

00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:23.790
Unlike the first batch, these bits were able
to be neutralized via regular bullets.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:28.970
Their search eventually bore fruit, and they
found the man patching himself up in a nearby

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:29.970
cellar.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:33.440
He had a briefcase, and the area around him
seemed to be a type of laboratory.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.250
Still, they were unable to find the silver
balloon anomaly.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:41.740
The operatives with weapons drawn, attempted
to speak with the man, but he lashed out and

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:46.040
shot at the them, prompting them to shoot
back, immediately killing him.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:51.040
They weren’t able to get much information
from him, but it was an act of self defense.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:55.010
The Foundation, now with their only source
of information gone, resorted to looking through

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.620
the rest of the basement.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:01.889
They found a series of documents held inside
the room, all written in Italian.

00:12:01.889 --> 00:12:06.139
They also found a tunnel leading outside the
town, and a small cart that was intended to

00:12:06.139 --> 00:12:10.760
be used to transport cylinders containing
the silver liquid out of Massarosa.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:15.300
The Foundation was very quick to stop this
anomaly from getting out on the black market,

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.790
as it seemed like this was a distribution
and testing center.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:24.250
But with the man dead and the gel contained,
they realized their mission was complete,

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:28.449
and collected all remaining documents and
traces of the silver liquid anomaly.

00:12:28.449 --> 00:12:33.149
In a joint effort between the Italian and
Lusophone branches, the liquid was transported

00:12:33.149 --> 00:12:39.930
to Brazil for further research and classified
as SCP-007-INT.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:46.970
The Lusophone branch’s board of superintendents
had made the decision earlier that SCP-007-INT

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:51.590
held historical and research significance
for the two branches, as some of the task

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:55.810
force members that aided in the capture of
the anomaly were sourced from Brazil.

00:12:55.810 --> 00:13:00.850
The documents were shared between both branches,
and chemical research on the object was conducted.

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:05.000
Immediately, the Foundation discovered the
reason why the liquid responded so quickly

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:10.269
to the man who was distributing it, and why
it works perfectly as a living shield.

00:13:10.269 --> 00:13:17.630
SCP-007-INT is sentient, and capable of recognizing
patterns and portraying emotion, albeit to

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.540
small degrees.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:25.769
Research into SCP-007-INT’s composition
and responses to stimuli in a lab environment

00:13:25.769 --> 00:13:30.120
continued, but one researcher from the Italian
branch noted that this wasn’t the first

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.839
time they had encountered an anomaly like
this.

00:13:32.839 --> 00:13:37.630
When dealing with a group of organizations
known as the Fascist Council of the Occult,

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:42.699
the Foundation discovered a heavily redacted
and secret anomalous weapon with certain properties

00:13:42.699 --> 00:13:45.060
similar to SCP-007-INT.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:50.830
While the details of this weapon were lost
to the database and above our clearance level,

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:55.529
we can assume that due to the nazi connection
between the man distributing the liquid and

00:13:55.529 --> 00:14:02.360
the fascist council of the occult, that portions
of SCP-007-INT managed to make their way to

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.930
the black market and proliferate the criminal
underworld.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:12.270
But when all the research was said and done,
what was SCP-007-INT?

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:17.570
The studies were conducted as a joint operation
between the two branches, and as a result,

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:20.830
allowed for a significant amount of testing.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.670
Researchers found that the gel was adaptable,
durable, and intelligent to a certain degree.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:30.560
But they also discovered that their data was
incredibly similar to another anomaly in their

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:35.800
database, recorded by the Lusophone branch’s
predecessor, the Scientific Academy of the

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:36.800
Anomalous.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.259
You see, the Foundation hasn’t been around
forever.

00:14:39.259 --> 00:14:44.709
Before it, the anomalous containment world
was decentralized and composed of tinier organizations,

00:14:44.709 --> 00:14:46.389
and this was one of them.

00:14:46.389 --> 00:14:53.459
As it turns out, this organization recorded
data remarkably similar to SCP-007-INT, but

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:57.960
the details of the research was lost due to
an incident involving rogue agents defecting

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:03.300
from the organization, think the Chaos Insurgency,
but before them too.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:09.889
The two instances of this anomaly were apparently
a perfect match to SCP-007-INT, and the two

00:15:09.889 --> 00:15:15.630
branches had both contained the same anomaly,
across decades, without being aware that the

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:16.800
other had done it.

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:21.491
While the documents were lost when the defecting
agents broke away from the Academy, researchers

00:15:21.491 --> 00:15:26.899
theorized that they either defected into or
sold information about the anomaly to the

00:15:26.899 --> 00:15:31.470
Fascist Council, who were able to improve
the liquid and turn it into a formidable,

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:33.180
military grade weapon.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:38.610
Still, the experiments with SCP-007-INT proved
to be a success.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:43.370
The anomaly’s sapience allowed it to form
a bond with its host, protecting and showing

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:46.009
the desire to comfort them if need be.

00:15:46.009 --> 00:15:48.380
What a nice little hunk of deadly gunk, right?

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:52.759
But then, just as the branches were about
to give up on finding the Academy’s old

00:15:52.759 --> 00:15:58.730
documentation for SCP-007-INT, they happened
to discover it.

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.010
The anomaly was given the codename “Project
Mel”.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:06.630
This initial research found that the anomaly
was incredibly adaptive, as seen below:

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:11.380
“Instance α is the most belligerent case
of SCP-007-INT.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:17.569
It prefers being involved in combat-oriented
exercises and watching martial performances.

00:16:17.569 --> 00:16:23.199
α has demonstrated a certain degree of infatuation
to the party with, in its conception, the

00:16:23.199 --> 00:16:28.610
best performance by using its pseudopods in
attempts to imitate some executed movements

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.519
for the respective party to see.”

00:16:30.519 --> 00:16:33.500
“Instance β is an exemplary case of personality.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:39.169
I have witnessed β adducting a stuffed penguin,
irresponsibly given by one of its Operators

00:16:39.169 --> 00:16:44.450
— to demonstrate affection; β also displayed
excitement when presented with pictures of

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.450
penguins.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:50.560
An extraordinary situation involving β happened
when it parted itself; its copy assumed the

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:56.310
form of a penguin, which β proceeded to care
for in the likeness of an animal companion.

00:16:56.310 --> 00:17:01.339
β protected and guided the copy through the
training course until the spontaneous expiration

00:17:01.339 --> 00:17:02.339
thereof.”

00:17:02.339 --> 00:17:06.400
“Instance γ possesses a particularly high
physical intelligence.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:12.350
It is expressly competent in solving movement-related
problematics such as obstacle courses involving

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:17.710
the manipulation of sensitive objects and
complex movement and transformation patterns.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:23.180
Interestingly, γ has been seen reacting to
music by dancing to the respective rhythm.”

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:28.010
This original documentation proved to be valuable
to the Foundation, as it provided further

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:34.520
information on what occurred when SCP-007-INT
was stolen from its original location and

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.920
placed into the hands of the Fascist Council.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:43.600
On December 25th, 1972, several security breaches
across the Academy occurred, as sleeper agents

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:49.110
of the Council stole various anomalous assets
from storehouses and vaults across the country.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:54.330
For two hours, the group of six rogue individuals
took what they could, smuggling the objects

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:59.420
away from the organization for the purposes
of using and selling them to the highest bidder.

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:03.840
Objects stolen included “Project Mel”,
several prototype prosthetics, and various

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:07.320
other pieces of high-security Academy documentation.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:12.100
The Foundation also discovered that these
sleeper agents within the Academy were students,

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:17.330
researchers, and operatives who had been working
with the organization for years, sometimes

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.420
decades.

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:22.580
Given their history, it's possible they may
have been coerced rather than them being outright

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:25.390
agents of the fascist council of the occult.

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:30.140
Unfortunately, all of them expired during
the interrogation procedures, and only one

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:35.210
survived, captured by the Academy via suspended
animation, though their whereabouts in the

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.000
present day are unknown.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:43.570
It’s unknown if the Foundation has seen
the last of SCP-007-INT, or if samples of

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:48.680
the deadly, adaptive living shield are still
lurking in the anomalous criminal underworld.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:56.590
Regardless, whoever possesses SCP-007-INT
is surely to be a formidable force for anyone

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.160
to go up against.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:04.040
Now go check out “SCP-354 - The Red Pool”
and “SCP-006 - Fountain of Youth” for

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:07.660
more anomalous liquids contained by the SCP
Foundation!

